WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.730
Paris, the 1890s.

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:11.590
A young Peruvian engineer, Pedro Paulet, later claimed he fired a liquid-fuel rocket engine here.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:17.930
He also drew a rocket craft of his own: the Avion-Torpedo.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:21.570
For more than a century, it stayed on paper.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:30.560
Arequipa, Peru. Three classmates wanted to go up there: Pedro, Chicho and Roberto.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:36.500
Years later, on a salsa night in Callao, they met Franchesca,

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:42.650
an astrobiologist back from the United States, looking for life in the Andes.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:47.040
<v Goicochea>If Paulet started it, why don't we finish it?

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:54.570
A small institute. An old notebook. A 130-year promise.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:00.770
Kuntur: Your seat is ready. Let's fly.

